---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center text-primary hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <img
          src="/BGILD.png"
          alt="BGILD Summer Institute Speaker"
          class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto h-64 object-cover rounded-2xl border border-neutral/20"
        />
      </div>
      <h1 class="mb-6 font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white">
        BGILD Summer Institute Speaker
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-neutral">
        My first official speaking engagement at the Black Girls in the Lead (BGILD) Summer Institute at the University of Ghana, delivering a hybrid session on practising leadership through community service.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">The Session</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Incredibly honoured to share that I had my first official speaking engagement at the Black Girls in the Lead (BGILD) Summer Institute at the University of Ghana. It was a privilege to speak alongside inspiring individuals such as Shamima Muslim and other notable speakers.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed mb-4">
          During my one-hour hybrid session on "Practising Leadership through Community Service," I shared my bee journey with brilliant young girls—from winning The National Spelling Bee Ghana in 2018 and being featured on CNN's African Voices, to my life afterwards, including founding Sage Literacy Foundation at thirteen and overcoming the initial obstacles I faced. I spoke about the true meaning of leadership and the importance of determination. It was a wonderful opportunity to discuss the impact of literacy and community service on personal growth and leadership.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">
          The feedback and warm reception I received were truly humbling, and I had a great time interacting with the girls. Thank you to Sisters Keepers for the invitation. This experience has further fuelled my passion for empowering others, and I look forward to more opportunities to share, learn, and grow.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="flex justify-center">
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7237724833982148608/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="rounded-full bg-primary px-8 py-4 text-white font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors after:ml-2 after:content-[url(/external.svg)]"
        >
          View on LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
